1
00:00:01,480 --> 00:00:03,740
Hello everyone and welcome to EnglishPod.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:04,400
My name is Marco.

3
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:08,400
My name is Catherine and today we are cleaning, right Marco?

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:09,180
That's right.

5
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:10,660
Today we are cleaning our house.

6
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:20,160
It's not one of our favorite activities but we have to do it and so we're going to take a look at a lot of great vocab related to household chores.

7
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:20,900
That's right.

8
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:22,560
So let's take a listen to today's dialogue.

9
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:30,440
Kevin, what is this mess?

10
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:32,280
It looks like a pigsty in here.

11
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:33,260
Clean this up.

12
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:34,780
Okay, dad.

13
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:36,040
I will do it in a minute.

14
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:37,760
Let me just finish this level of this game.

15
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,100
No, I said now.

16
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:40,480
Plus, you are grounded.

17
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:42,180
You're not allowed to play video games.

18
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:46,820
I want you to make your bed, do the laundry and then come downstairs and sweep the floors.

19
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:48,380
That's so unfair.

20
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:50,960
You have to pull your weight around here, young man.

21
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:52,620
My house, my rules.

22
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:57,400
And I already mopped the floors, dusted the furniture and vacuumed the rugs.

23
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:59,680
That's great but you still have work to do so get to it.

24
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:08,750
So today on Language Takeaway, let's take a look at all the verbs and all the ways that we have to clean the house.

25
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,190
So starting with the first one, we have to make the bed, make your bed.

26
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:14,580
Make your bed.

27
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:21,320
Okay, so this might sound quite strange because the verb to make is something we say for a lot of different things like make a deal.

28
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:22,020
Make a mistake.

29
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:23,680
Make a mistake.

30
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:24,380
But here, we're making the bed.

31
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:31,360
That means we're putting the pillows on top of the bed and we're going to make sure the blanket is even.

32
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:37,500
So when you get out of bed, if everything is very messy, when you make it, you put everything in order on your bed.

33
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:38,200
That's right.

34
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:40,080
That's right.

35
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:43,440
And well, it's also confusing because our next verb is to do the laundry.

36
00:01:43,690 --> 00:01:44,230
All right.

37
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:47,770
So you make your bed but you do the laundry.

38
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:51,310
The laundry here means you clean the dirty clothes.

39
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:52,210
Right, right.

40
00:01:52,920 --> 00:02:02,710
So this is one of the very, I would say, confusing parts of English where it's kind of confusing when to use the verb make, when to use the verb do.

41
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:10,470
So usually, you make a mistake as we say or you make a cake but you do your homework.

42
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:16,650
So in these cases, you just kind of have to memorize that you make the bed but you do the laundry.

43
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:18,240
Exactly.

44
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:20,800
So this is very common actually to do the laundry.

45
00:02:20,950 --> 00:02:24,490
I have to go do the laundry today because it's an event.

46
00:02:25,090 --> 00:02:30,440
You know, you have to gather your clothes and put in the detergent and wash it and dry it.

47
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:35,480
So just remember, make the bed, do the laundry but then how do we clean those floors?

48
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:36,340
All right.

49
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:39,140
So the floor, we have to do two things.

50
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:41,600
We sweep the floors.

51
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:43,020
So the verb there is to sweep.

52
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:45,120
And how do you sweep?

53
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:48,040
You actually use a broom to sweep.

54
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:51,000
So the broom is like a straw.

55
00:02:51,700 --> 00:03:00,460
It's like a brush almost that you use on the floor and you collect all of the hair and the dust and these things and you put it into the garbage bin.

56
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:09,280
But after you sweep, then you need to use water to clean because obviously, sweeping is just for dry things.

57
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:12,600
Mopping is actually how you clean with water and soap.

58
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:12,740
That's right.

59
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:20,360
So now the verb there is to mop the floors and usually, you use water, you use soap and you use a mop.

60
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:21,380
So you use a mop to mop.

61
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:22,720
Exactly.

62
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:23,380
The verb is to mop.

63
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:27,240
The noun, the object is a mop like you say.

64
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:30,020
So I'm going to mop the floors, right?

65
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:32,260
So please don't come into the kitchen.

66
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:33,800
Right.

67
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:34,800
Right.

68
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:35,800
Okay.

69
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:41,300
And well, now we need to clean the furniture and usually, on the furniture, we have a lot of dust.

70
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:43,800
So we need to dust the furniture, to dust.

71
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:44,700
To dust.

72
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:50,320
Yeah, this is something we don't use for the floors really because we have this great verb to sweep.

73
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:58,180
But with furniture and things like that, we say to dust and this means we're going to collect the dust off of the piano or the sofa or the table.

74
00:03:58,640 --> 00:03:59,640
Right.

75
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:00,640
Exactly.

76
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:16,640
And now, the floors we clean, the furniture we clean, but sometimes we have rugs or we have carpet in our house, usually in the bedrooms or we have a large rug in the living room and we need to clean that as well, but we don't really mop it and we don't sweep it.

77
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,230
It's best to vacuum it.

78
00:04:18,610 --> 00:04:18,990
All right.

79
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:23,130
So the verb is to vacuum and what is the noun, the thing we use?

80
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:24,560
A vacuum cleaner.

81
00:04:24,590 --> 00:04:27,050
A vacuum cleaner or just simply a vacuum.

82
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:33,120
Now this is something that uses air to suck up all of the dirt and garbage.

83
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:38,520
So it goes and it sucks up all of that bad stuff and so we don't have to dust it.

84
00:04:38,520 --> 00:04:40,730
And obviously, with carpet, we can't really use water.

85
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:42,040
Exactly.

86
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:46,160
So carpet is a great tool for cleaning fabric like carpets and rugs.

87
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,160
Very good.

88
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:52,550
So that's all the ways that we can basically, the verbs that we use to clean around the house.

89
