It looks like a pigsty in here.

92
00:05:05,010 --> 00:05:05,770
Clean this up.

93
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:07,300
Okay, dad.

94
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:08,560
I will do it in a minute.

95
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:10,280
Let me just finish this level of this game.

96
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:10,700
No.

97
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:13,020
Now, plus you are grounded.

98
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:14,740
You're not allowed to play video games.

99
00:05:15,180 --> 00:05:19,340
I want you to make your bed, do the laundry and then come downstairs and sweep the floors.

100
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:20,920
That's so unfair.

101
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:23,500
You have to pull your weight around here, young man.

102
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:25,160
My house, my rules.

103
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:29,220
But I already mopped the floors, dusted the furniture and vacuumed the rugs.

104
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:32,220
That's great, but you still have work to do, so get to it.

105
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:39,030
All right, so now let's take a look at some phrases, three of them on Fluency Builder.

106
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:45,640
All right, now the first word here is pigsty.

107
00:05:45,940 --> 00:05:49,120
The dad says, Kevin, it looks like a pigsty in here.

108
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:50,380
Clean this up.

109
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:52,140
Right, so a pigsty.

110
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:53,100
It looks like a pigsty.

111
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:57,000
Now, a pigsty is where pigs live, right?

112
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:57,140
That's right.

113
00:05:57,460 --> 00:05:59,140
So, is it really a pigsty?

114
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:00,980
It's not really a pigsty.

115
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:07,520
There are no pigs living there, but to say that a room is like a pigsty means that it's very, very, very dirty.

116
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:07,760
Right.

117
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:12,400
It looks almost like the mud and the dirty place where pigs live.

118
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:12,920
Exactly.

119
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:16,400
So, he's saying, you're living in a dirty room.

120
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:17,100
You need to clean this.

121
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:18,560
Right.

122
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:22,200
So, a room or a house will look like a pigsty.

123
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:29,640
Now, the dad is actually making him do a lot of work because he says the kid is grounded.

124
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:30,100
You're grounded.

125
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:32,460
You're not allowed to play video games.

126
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:40,260
Now, a parent will ground a child, it's a verb, when the child does something bad.

127
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:41,800
Right.

128
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:48,740
So, maybe the child gets very, very bad grades at school and the parent says, ugh, you're grounded for one week.

129
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:51,840
That means you can't go out, you can't play video games.

130
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:59,440
There are different rules in every family, but to say you're grounded means you're being punished for something.

131
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,440
Right.

132
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:03,780
So, the verb is to ground and you can also be grounded.

133
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:07,580
And if you're grounded, you can say, I'm sorry, I can't go out today, I'm grounded.

134
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:08,760
Exactly.

135
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:15,420
So, to be grounded is not a fun situation, but obviously the father is saying, listen, you're grounded.

136
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,780
You have time to do all of this work.

137
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:19,520
Right.

138
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:24,560
And well, this is something that my dad used to say to me, well, you have to pull your weight around here.

139
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:26,720
So, you have to pull your weight around here.

140
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:27,200
What does that mean?

141
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:28,500
To pull your weight.

142
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:37,220
Well, you think about it, if you're not carrying yourself, someone else is carrying you, it means that they're doing more work than they should be.

143
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:38,520
Right.

144
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:47,480
So, you're basically being asked to do your part, to be responsible for yourself so that other people like your mom and dad don't have to be responsible for you.

145
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:47,860
Right.

146
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:50,640
So, you have to help out and collaborate.

147
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:50,920
Exactly.

148
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:56,280
So, say there's three people, mom, dad, and a son.

149
00:07:56,280 --> 00:08:02,520
If mom does all the cleaning, all the cooking, all the washing, then the other two, they're not pulling their weight.

150
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:05,500
So, she says, pull your weight, do some cleaning, do some washing.

151
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:06,920
Right.

152
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:10,940
So, if your mom cooks and then you wash the dishes, then you are pulling your weight.

153
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:11,440
You're helping.

154
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:12,360
You're helping out.

155
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:12,920
Exactly.

156
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:15,120
All right.

157
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:16,120
A lot of great stuff.

158
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:19,520
Let's take a listen to the dialogue one last time.

159
00:08:23,910 --> 00:08:25,450
Kevin, what is this mess?

160
00:08:25,750 --> 00:08:27,270
It looks like a pigsty in here.

161
00:08:27,510 --> 00:08:28,230
Clean this up.

162
00:08:29,030 --> 00:08:29,790
Okay, dad.

163
00:08:30,090 --> 00:08:31,030
I will do it in a minute.

164
00:08:31,230 --> 00:08:32,750
Let me just finish this level of this game.

165
00:08:32,990 --> 00:08:34,110
No, I said now.

166
00:08:34,530 --> 00:08:35,490
Plus, you are grounded.

167
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,190
You're not allowed to play video games.

168
00:08:37,630 --> 00:08:41,810
I want you to make your bed, do the laundry, and then come downstairs and sweep the floors.

169
00:08:42,310 --> 00:08:43,390
That's so unfair.

170
00:08:44,210 --> 00:08:45,970
You have to pull your weight around here, young man.

171
00:08:46,230 --> 00:08:47,630
My house, my rules.

172
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:51,690
But I already mopped the floors, dusted the furniture, and vacuumed the rugs.

173
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,690
That's great, but you still have work to do, so get to it.

174
00:08:59,430 --> 00:09:00,550
Okay, very good.

175
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:04,080
So, doing household chores, not a fun thing.

176
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:05,470
But also, being grounded.

177
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:08,850
Why do we consider chores to be kind of like a punishment?

178
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:15,520
Well, there's punishment where you sit alone in your room and you think about your actions, and then there's punishment that's more proactive.

179
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:18,740
Mom and dad say, okay, well, he's grounded.

180
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,020
Let's have him work.

181
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:21,640
Let's make him do something.

182
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:25,540
Let's make him do something so that we're benefiting from his punishment.

183
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:32,380
I think it's also good when children are grounded because it makes them realize that they need to help out around the house.

184
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:35,760
This work, it doesn't get done magically.

185
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,600
There's actually someone doing it.

186
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:39,040
Right.

187
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:53,950
And it's not like, well, in many cases in many countries, people will have, like we saw in our previous lesson, a domestic maid, a cleaning lady, that will usually do everything so maybe the kid will become very comfortable and not really do anything.

188
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:55,240
Or very lazy.

189
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:56,240
Very lazy.

190
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:57,240
Even worse, yeah.

191
00:09:57,240 --> 00:10:06,680
So, I definitely remember in my house we had chores because when it's not punishment, when it's your parents' expectation normally, that's called a chore.

192
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:14,340
And they say, okay, Catherine, your chores this week, you need to take the garbage outside, you need to wash the dishes, and you need to make your bed every day.

193
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:21,600
And then maybe my brother had to help cook and clean the floor, mop the floors and sweep.

194
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,520
So we have different chores.

195
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:25,120
Right.

196
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:31,740
And I guess this is more common especially if both parents work and everyone is collaborating or pulling their weight in the house.

197
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:34,560
And if you don't have a cleaning lady, for example.

198
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,200
Exactly.

